Port patch 0034 - calls compiled with the wrong signature (found while building the game as WebAssembly for the Switch and Android port)
Why: a function that is called without a prototype in scope (or through a wrong declaration) is compiled as `int f()` with the arguments of the call. On the console that never mattered: MIPS passes the first four arguments in registers whatever the callee declares and a result nobody reads is harmless. WebAssembly checks function types: the linker replaces a call whose type differs from the definition with a stub that traps at run time. 14 functions were affected (PokeIcon_OpenModelArchives, Audio_FadeCategoriesAndStreamsDefault/WithDuration, GbSave_MarkBoxDataLoaded, GbSave_SetSeenOwnedBits, LabPC_ShowBoxes, Text_LoadPlayerLabels, func_80033B2C, func_800361C4, func_81209078, HAL_Printf (profiler.c, util.c), Display_ClearFramebufferLine, Ui_DrawTextureMarker, and _bcopy in libleo/bootdisk.c).
How: each caller gets the real prototype. Two calls passed an argument the callee ignores (Display_ClearFramebufferLine in reset.c, Ui_DrawTextureMarker in minigame_select); the extra argument is dropped. The header of the Game Boy Tower fragment declared func_81209078 as void although it returns s32. No change in behaviour on the native builds.

